  url: {{baseUrl}}/v2.2/acl
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
{
  "acl": [
    {
      "cidr": "203.0.113.0/24"
    }
  ]
}
}

docs {
**Remove IP ACL entries**
Removes ACL entries. The live handler reads the same JSON body as POST /v2.2/acl — sent as a request body with DELETE (the v2.2.0 rewrite): {"acl": [{"cidr": "203.0.113.0/24"}, ...]} . An address without a mask is /32; entries are matched exactly, and entries that do not exist fail individually. (The body is described here rather than as a requestBody node: DELETE-with-body is discouraged style, but it is the wire truth.)

Returns **200 OK** with a JSON body (not 204).

OperationId: `aclDelete`
}
